{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar","id":918274,"title":"Help making a Resistance focused Solar","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-20T15:33:40-07:00","id":918274,"title":"Help making a Resistance focused Solar","content":"This is the first time im going to make a Solar focused on Resistance. Im not sure what charms to pick because until now i havent touched anything beyond ox-body and Body-Mending<br /> Meditation.<br /> I have heard that you cant really understand how awsome the Resistance charm are with just a read through the book, and that it is even possible to be almost unkillable if you go deep into resistance and a little of either parry or defence.<br /> So, how does the interplay between the different charms works? How can i make an unkillable monster?<br /> Also, that picture of a soldier breaking his hammer on Panther. What charm/combination of charms would that be?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T15:51:26-07:00","id":918281,"title":"","content":"Buy up to Aegis and you have basically all the pieces you need. I'd also recommend Dodge ( Shadow over Water, Leaping Dodge Technique) to cover weaknesses that Resistance alone has.<br /> <br /> <br /> Breaking the hammer... honestly the only thing that comes to mind is that Craft Charm - Object-Shattering Touch? I'm totally blanking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T16:02:03-07:00","id":918285,"title":"","content":"Your go-to defence is Iron Kettle Body. Paired with a high soak and the upgrades unlocked by a Resistance Supernal, only extremely damaging withering attacks will trouble you. It seems expensive, but when you consider that you can just <i>not defend</i> against a lot of attacks and watch them ping off your steely abs, you will reap a lot back in excellency dice you didn't spend, particularly if you are facing multiple attackers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T16:27:28-07:00","id":918296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar#post918274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the first time im going to make a Solar focused on Resistance. Im not sure what charms to pick because until now i havent touched anything beyond ox-body and Body-Mending<br /> Meditation.<br /> I have heard that you cant really understand how awsome the Resistance charm are with just a read through the book, and that it is even possible to be almost unkillable if you go deep into resistance and a little of either parry or defence.<br /> So, how does the interplay between the different charms works? How can i make an unkillable monster?<br /> Also, that picture of a soldier breaking his hammer on Panther. What charm/combination of charms would that be?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Favor Brawl and a few more esoteric Abilities, like Athletics, Dodge, or Lore. Brawl gives you unarmed Clashes, Athletics gives you better Feats of Strength, and Dodge gives you damage conversion into Initiative, motes, or Willpower.<br /> If I had to guess, he's stunting a feat of strength after using Snake Strikes the Heel with Fire-Eating Fist to launch a Disarm attempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T16:39:40-07:00","id":918305,"title":"","content":"The thing to remember about Resistance is that, while Soak can be immensely strong, it's not set up to be equally good as parry or dodge. There's no charm that will turn you into Superman and let you just parry every attack with your face, forever. This is because Soak is a second tier defense, used to mitigate the results of you failing to block or dodge.<br /> <br /> As such, ironically, the first thing you should look into is Dodge or Parry. At the very least you want an excellency and maybe something to negate penalties.<br /> <br /> After that, it's time to look at Resistance. Starting with Ox-Body, it's important to note that every HL you have means your opponent needs to build up 2 to 3 more initiative before they can kill you. Which means that, as long as your Stamina is above 3, each time you take Ox-Body, your opponent needs about 9 more init to kill you. And, past a certain point, it can be hard to build up to that. Also, the Pain Tolerance Merit will turn all of your -2 HLs into -1s, which will be really handy.<br /> <br /> Something else to consider is whether you want to wear armor or not. Several of the best soak boosting charms in Resistance are specifically incompatible with armor. You can grab Artifact armor and the armor boosting charms or go for charms that simply boost your soak. I'm not sure which is better off hand, but I did work on a character that specifically didn't wear armor once, so I'm gonna give advice in that direction.<br /> <br /> The thing to remember about being Soak focused is that, in 3e, it means 1) you're going to get hit and 2) it's going to hurt. Resistance charms are there to help you manage how hurt you get, not to prevent you from getting hurt. Durability of Oak Meditation is a good example. Like other defense charms, it needs to be invoked before the attack roll, so, it's not there to save you after you get hit. It's there to help you boost your soak a bit so you only take min damage if they hit you or to help blunt the damage a bit when your opponent unleashes their mega damage combo. Also, because of the damage reduction, it gives you an effective six hardness against Decisive Attacks. As some builds use charms to increase their base init rating then spam 4-5 damage Decisive attacks, this shuts down all of those tactics cold.<br /> <br /> As for specific charm advice, many Resistance charms are a bit on the expensive side, so Essence-Gathering Temper is a good buy. Ox-Body *2 and Body Mending Meditation are a must. If you're going unarmored, then Diamond Body Prana and it's prereqs are essential. If you really want to be &quot;Dude who can shrug off a Goremaul to the face,&quot; then I'd advise grabbing Adamant Skin Technique. Alternately, Tiger Warrior's Endurance will give you free healing whenever you recover from being crashed, so, if you think that might happen fairly often, that might be something to look at. If you have charms left, look at Ruin-Abasing Shrug and Wound-Knitting Exercise.<br /> <br /> If you want to be a berserker, Battle Fury Focus and Blood Thirst Sword-Dancer Spirit will give you some pretty impressive combat buffs, at the cost of you being unable to stop fighting willingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 06-20-2016, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T16:44:23-07:00","id":918311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=918285#post918285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your go-to defence is Iron Kettle Body. Paired with a high soak and the upgrades unlocked by a Resistance Supernal, only extremely damaging withering attacks will trouble you. It seems expensive, but when you consider that you can just <i>not defend</i> against a lot of attacks and watch them ping off your steely abs, you will reap a lot back in excellency dice you didn't spend, particularly if you are facing multiple attackers.</div> </div> </div> </div>....Are you thinking of Spirit-Strengthens the Skin?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T17:00:55-07:00","id":918318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=918311#post918311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ....Are you thinking of Spirit-Strengthens the Skin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Iron Kettle Body halves all post-soak withering damage before it is rolled for one turn, and with Supernal Resistance (or high Essence) drains Initiative from your opponent to you.<br /> <br /> With a cost of 6m and a requirement that it be activated before the attack is rolled, I did not think much of it at first; but Crumplepunch has been using it to some great effectiveness and I have since revised my assessment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 06-20-2016, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T17:27:14-07:00","id":918336,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your answers. So, Iron Kettle Body would be the meat of the defence then, and the rest of the charms make my character more godly?<br /> she may apply her<br /> I just read that Adamant Skin Technique applys my full (Stamina + armor soak) to a decisive attack. Does that mean that i substract Stamina + armor soak from the initiative rolled for the atack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T18:05:28-07:00","id":918352,"title":"","content":"Yes, that's correct. Though in my experience Durability of Oak Meditation has been just as much a &quot;meat and potatoes&quot; defense as Iron Kettle Body has - remember that DoOM is a tick long, so anyone going at the same time as your first attacker is going to have their damage reduced as well. The more people go at once, the more it pays for itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T20:01:05-07:00","id":918392,"title":"","content":"If you want to have fun, combine Aegis of Invincible Might/your powerful Resistance Charm of choice, Essence-Gathering Temper, and War Lion Stance.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying I, as a GM, cried.<br /> <br /> But I'm not <b>not</b> saying that I cried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T20:16:37-07:00","id":918397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=918336#post918336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just read that Adamant Skin Technique applys my full (Stamina + armor soak) to a decisive attack. Does that mean that i substract Stamina + armor soak from the initiative rolled for the atack?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the (Initiative) damage pool, yes. Awesome, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Also Shattering Grasp is the Charm I was thinking of that lets you disassemble things with a touch.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T20:19:40-07:00","id":918398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar#post918274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, that picture of a soldier breaking his hammer on Panther.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is this picture and does it have any dialogue balloons (yet)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T20:33:36-07:00","id":918403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=918398#post918398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is this picture and does it have any dialogue balloons (yet)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted 3rd Edition, page 375.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, right bellow!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimage.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://s31.postimg.org/rh79u7wor/Hammer_Ti_O_O.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> As for how Panther is doing that, I don't think there is any particular &quot;break things on my body&quot; Charms involved, just part of a stunt for his fight against that battlegroup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 06-20-2016, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T20:40:45-07:00","id":918406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=918403#post918403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalted 3rd Edition, page 375.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, right bellow!</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/F12HVOm.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T22:16:06-07:00","id":918446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=918305#post918305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no charm that will turn you into Superman and let you just parry every attack with your face, forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I hope when Infernals hit the on-deck circle there's still a Resistance Charm like Ablation of Brass and Fire, even if it's too costly to use often. That was my favorite Charm in all of 2nd Edition.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T22:41:33-07:00","id":918449,"title":"","content":"I maintain that he's using the Brawl/MA combo I mentioned above, because Clashing seems to be the better way to simulate that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T01:41:57-07:00","id":918498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=918311#post918311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ....Are you thinking of Spirit-Strengthens the Skin?</div> </div> </div> </div>SStS backs up Iron Kettle Body quite nicely if you find yourself being overpowered and need to up your soak, but no, I meant what I said.<br /> <br /> Allow me to back it up. Here is an attack between two starting characters in a recent game of mine, a Snake fighter and a Resistance Supernal.<br /> <br /> Snake fighter (Strength 2, Dexterity 5, Martial Arts 5, Unarmed speciality) does a finger jab attack against the Resistance Supernal (Dexterity 3, Stamina 5, Brawl 5, Unarmed speciality),. This particular character is unarmoured, so she has Diamond Body Prana up.<br /> <br /> <b>10 10 8 8 7</b> 6 5 2 1 1<br /> <br /> A good start, 7 successes on DBP means a total soak of 15.<br /> <br /> Now, the attack. The Snake fighter goes all in and uses a full MA excellency (10m) and Striking Cobra Technique (3m), her strongest attack.<br /> <br /> 21 dice from base pool and excellency, 4 from unarmed accuracy, and another 2 from a stunt. 27. Brawler stunts a defence for a total defence of 6 and activates Iron Kettle Body.<br /> <br /> <b>10 10 9 9 9 8 7 7 7 7</b> 6 6 6 6 5 5 5 4 4 3 3 3 2 2 1 1 1<br /> <br /> That's 12 successes, 6 threshold. There are 3 1s, so the brawler steals 3 initiative from her attacker.<br /> <br /> Raw damage of the attack is 25. Brawler activates Essence Gathering Temper to gain 10m from the attack at the cost of 1i.<br /> <br /> Soak reduces the attack to 10, which is then halved to 5 by IKB.<br /> <br /> <b>9 7 7</b> 3 3<br /> <br /> 3 successes. Brawler uses Spirit Strengthens the Skin's second mode to negate the damage at the cost of 6m, 1wp, 2i. Essence Gathering Temper is reset.<br /> <br /> So, at a final count:<br /> <br /> Snake Fighter loses: 13m, 2i.<br /> <br /> Brawler loses: 2m, 1wp.<br /> <br /> Snake fighter breaks her fingers and Iron Kettle Body is active for the rest of the action.<br /> <br /> Of course there are attacks against which this defence is not effective, but unless your opponent has a method of doing superior amounts of damage, you can tank through it using these Charms and lose little if any initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 06-21-2016, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T08:06:24-07:00","id":918626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=918498#post918498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> SStS backs up Iron Kettle Body quite nicely if you find yourself being overpowered and need to up your soak, but no, I meant what I said.<br /> <br /> Allow me to back it up. Here is an attack between two starting characters in a recent game of mine, a Snake fighter and a Resistance Supernal.<br /> <br /> Snake fighter (Strength 2, Dexterity 5, Martial Arts 5, Unarmed speciality) does a finger jab attack against the Resistance Supernal (Dexterity 3, Stamina 5, Brawl 5, Unarmed speciality),. This particular character is unarmoured, so she has Diamond Body Prana up.<br /> <br /> <b>10 10 8 8 7</b> 6 5 2 1 1<br /> <br /> A good start, 7 successes on DBP means a total soak of 15.<br /> <br /> Now, the attack. The Snake fighter goes all in and uses a full MA excellency (10m) and Striking Cobra Technique (3m), her strongest attack.<br /> <br /> 21 dice from base pool and excellency, 4 from unarmed accuracy, and another 2 from a stunt. 27. Brawler stunts a defence for a total defence of 6 and activates Iron Kettle Body.<br /> <br /> <b>10 10 9 9 9 8 7 7 7 7</b> 6 6 6 6 5 5 5 4 4 3 3 3 2 2 1 1 1<br /> <br /> That's 12 successes, 6 threshold. There are 3 1s, so the brawler steals 3 initiative from her attacker.<br /> <br /> Raw damage of the attack is 25. Brawler activates Essence Gathering Temper to gain 10m from the attack at the cost of 1i.<br /> <br /> Soak reduces the attack to 10, which is then halved to 5 by IKB.<br /> <br /> <b>9 7 7</b> 3 3<br /> <br /> 3 successes. Brawler uses Spirit Strengthens the Skin's second mode to negate the damage at the cost of 6m, 1wp, 2i. Essence Gathering Temper is reset.<br /> <br /> So, at a final count:<br /> <br /> Snake Fighter loses: 13m, 2i.<br /> <br /> Brawler loses: 2m, 1wp.<br /> <br /> Snake fighter breaks her fingers and Iron Kettle Body is active for the rest of the action.<br /> <br /> Of course there are attacks against which this defence is not effective, but unless your opponent has a method of doing superior amounts of damage, you can tank through it using these Charms and lose little if any initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Brb, respeccing all my characters as Resistance supernal now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Pronounced &quot;Monkey Pie&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/762726-actual-play-the-party-prelude-project\" target=\"_blank\">Find my actual play content here!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/656-monkipi","name":"Monkipi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar656_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"318"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T12:41:14-07:00","id":918748,"title":"","content":"I personally think that Tiger Warrior's Endurance, and Wound Knitting Exercise are two of the most powerful charms available to a Resistance Supernal character as they will make it VERY hard to kill you with the armor, or non-armor soak increases possible but you will also need Stamina 5, and Ox Body Technique to take real advantage of them though. <br /> <br /> <b>For example at Essence 1, Stamina 5, Resistance Supernal</b><br /> Having 12 x -0 health levels, and 7 x -1 health levels, 7 x -2 health levels<br /> -The -0's heal 1 per 2 rounds when you spend a simple action to begin healing them...the -1's or -2's to heal whenever you recover from Initiative crash once per scene...<br /> <br /> This does cost an obscene number of charms for the full kit however, as it will cost you 13 charms to basically become Immortal, so you might want to try a smaller commitment first to see if you like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T12:56:15-07:00","id":918757,"title":"","content":"It has been brought to my attention that I actually completely messed that damage calculation up. The raw damage of the attack should have been a mere 19, reduced to 4 by soak and 2 by IKB, then negated with 1wp, 4m, 2i. The final loss to the Brawler should have been only 1wp.<br /> <br /> To test the limitations of this defence, here's a far more formidable withering attack. A Melee Supernal with a Grand Daiklave and 5 Strength, Strength Increasing Exercise. Characters are E1.<br /> <br /> Melee fighter is using Melee Excellency (8m) Excellent Strike (3m) and Fire and Stones Strike (6m). Our Brawler has traded in her Diamond Body Prana for a suit of artifact heavy plate.<br /> <br /> Attack pool is 22 + 1 automatic success. Defence (Brawl Parry) is 6, Brawler uses Iron Kettle Body.<br /> <br /> <b>10 10 10 10 9 7 7</b> 6 6 5 5 5 4 4 4 4 3 2 2 1 1 1/<b>9</b> 6 2<br /> <br /> 11 successes, 1 on a reroll, an average roll, but it misses out on activating Rising Sun slash (no 8s). Because Excellent Strike rerolled the 1s, the Brawler steals no initiative. 6 threshold successes.<br /> <br /> Damage is 26, reduced to 10 by soak, then increased back to 16 by Fire and Stones Strike, and halved back to 8 by Iron Kettle Body. The brawler spends 1i on Essence-Gathering Temper to gain 10m.<br /> <br /> <b>9 9 8 8 </b>5 3 3 2<br /> <br /> 4 damage, another average roll. Negated for 8m, 2i, 1wp by Spirit Strengthens the Skin. Essence-Gathering Temper is reset.<br /> <br /> Final costs:<br /> <br /> Brawler: 4m, 1wp, 3i.<br /> Melee Supernal: 17m. Gains 1i.<br /> <br /> So yeah, using this combination with a Resistance Supernal it seems you are highly resistant to even the most damaging conventional withering attacks as long as you have enough willpower to negate the final damage and reset Essence-Gathering Temper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 06-21-2016, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T13:09:11-07:00","id":918763,"title":"","content":"I was about to call you out on the Brawler stealing init from the attack, but you edited too fast","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T13:10:45-07:00","id":918766,"title":"","content":"Also I'm pretty sure Essence-Gathering Temper cannot be reset on the same attack it was triggered from. That is insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T13:16:21-07:00","id":918767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=918766#post918766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I'm pretty sure Essence-Gathering Temper cannot be reset on the same attack it was triggered from. That is insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, you may be right, but that just means you have to alternate using and resetting it between attacks. Both are pretty reliable; gain motes with EGT, negate damage with SStS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T13:29:45-07:00","id":918776,"title":"","content":"If the melee guy does 4 damage and brawler has heavy artifact armor, doesn't the damage becomes zero because of hardiness?<br /> <br /> <br /> And how does Diamond-Body Prana balances against using artifact armor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T13:39:26-07:00","id":918785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=918776#post918776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the melee guy does 4 damage and brawler has heavy artifact armor, doesn't the damage becomes zero because of hardiness?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, hardness only functions against decisive damage in Ex3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=918776#post918776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how does Diamond-Body Prana balances against using artifact armor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, I guess. DBP grants soak equal to ((Higher of Essence or 3) + (Rolled Stamina + Resistance)), so until E4 you'll get an average of 8 (assuming a maxed Resistance Stamina pool, which you really want for these Charms), slightly inferior to Medium artifact armour, better than Light. By E5, your average will be 10, just shy of Heavy.<br /> <br /> I don't really like the random element of it or the fact that it is a Simple Charm that eats an action to set up, but it's pretty functional. Its main advantage over heavy armour is that it is unobtrusive, does not inflict a mobility penalty and is compatible with Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> What bugs me the most about DBP is that the best decisive defences in Resistance are locked behind it, so even if you don't want to use it, tough, you've got to buy it if you want Adamant Skin Technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 06-21-2016, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T13:47:25-07:00","id":918787,"title":"","content":"Since a stunt may enhance any rolled action, and spending a WP on roll adds one automatic success, it is possible to stunt the [Stamina + Resistance] roll, so a major stunt or higher and a WP gives you heavy armor stats at E3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T14:46:35-07:00","id":918810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monkipi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=918626#post918626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brb, respeccing all my characters as Resistance supernal now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saddened that doing so doesn't really fit my character concept, but you can bet I'll be dipping into that tree of Resistance Charms pretty early.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T15:30:04-07:00","id":918835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=918785#post918785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, hardness only functions against decisive damage in Ex3.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, i had a brain fart and forgot this was withering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T05:29:15-07:00","id":919047,"title":"","content":"Adamant Skin Technique is compatible with Bronze skin, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T08:26:15-07:00","id":919101,"title":"","content":"Yes, but Diamond Body Prana isn't, since Invulnerable Skin of Bronze acts like wearing armor for the purpose of Charms that care if you're wearing armor or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T23:50:20-07:00","id":919546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=918285#post918285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when you consider that you can just <i>not defend</i> against a lot of attacks and watch them ping off your steely abs</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. I am so turned on by that image.<br /> <br /> Not sure if I want to make that character so I can date him, or play him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T05:51:34-07:00","id":919662,"title":"","content":"In rpg.net i saw a post made by OnyxHope that was asking about stacking some charms to get outrageous amounts of soak.<br /> Is this correct?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OnyxHope in rpg.net</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Not for any character I am planning to play right away but I had an odd set of stacking questions someone in the thread might be able to double-check my math on.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Lets say we are creating a starting Solar Zenith or Dawn with Resistance as their Supernal who at character creation is a terrestrial circle sorcerer with Stamina 5.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Pillar of the East</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> as we will call her takes Invulnerable Skin of Bronze as her Control Spell (and only one at this time) [1 charm Occult]</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">She takes the following Resistance Charms [7 charms], the re-purchase of Glorious Solar Plate to unlock her first Evocation from it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Durability of Oak</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Spirit Strengthens the Skin </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Whirlwind Armor-Donning Prana</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Armored Scout Invigoration</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Hauberk-Summoning Gesture</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Glorious Solar Plate (x2)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I understand that the following would be true for attacks that make it though her Parry/Evasion defense:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">If she is surprised and unable to summon either of her defenses (can you use Glorious Solar Plate a reflexive charm in your defense?):</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">5 natural Soak from Stamina, +1 for ISoB as Control Spell. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Total Natural Soak 6, no default Hardness</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">She can spend 3 motes to activate Durability of Oak meditation if desired to eat 2 of the opponents raw damage dice.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">For Withering attacks she could spend up to 6 motes to raise her natural soak to a maximum of 12 (5 for Stamina and 1 for ISoB which counts as natural) using Spirit Strengthens the Skin.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">For Decisive attacks Durability of Oak would give her 4 Hardness.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">If she has had time to shape Invulnerable Skin of Bronze and it is up then:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">5 natural Soak from Stamina, +7 natural Soak for ISoB and Unarmored</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Total Natural Soak 12, 7 Hardness</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">She can spend 3 motes to activate Durability of Oak meditation if desired to eat 2 of the opponents raw damage dice. (still)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">For Withering attacks she could spend up to 12! motes to raise her natural soak to a maximum of 24 (5 for Stamina and 7 for ISoB which counts as natural) using Spirit Strengthens the Skin.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">For Decisive attacks Durability of Oak would give her no additional Hardness. (higher hardness trumps, no stacking called out in charm)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Finally, if she takes the time to summon the blinding glory of her Glorious Solar Plate:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">5 natural Soak from Stamina, +6 natural Soak for ISoB and +11 Soak for GSP</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Total Soak 22, 10 Hardness</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">She can spend 3 motes to activate Durability of Oak meditation if desired to eat 2 of the opponents raw damage dice. (still)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">For Withering attacks she could spend up to 11 motes to raise her natural soak to a maximum of 22 (5 for Stamina and 6 for ISoB which counts as natural) using Spirit Strengthens the Skin. She gets a lower cap due to being armored but still has a higher soak overall when using it mote for mote.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">For Decisive attacks Durability of Oak would give her no additional Hardness. (higher hardness trumps, no stacking called out in charm)</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">When using SStS's maximum in each scenario we have a Soak of:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">12 unprepared but spending 6m on SStS</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">24 with only ISoB spending 12m on SStS</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">33 with everything up and spending 11m on SStS</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I am curious if this looks correct and also if there are many times where 35 effective soak (2 dice eaten from DoOM + full SStS) would ever come up in a starting Solar game, seems like a lot of overkill esp if she had any Brawl/Melee/Dodge charms to boost her Defense before raw damage.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T06:33:01-07:00","id":919676,"title":"","content":"Skimming over it, this seems accurate, as written it is possible to ratchet up a hell of a lot of soak. If you want a quick fix on this, I suggest that non-permanent enhancements to soak with a duration longer than an action should not stack. That stops unscrupulous martial artist sorcerers from piling up Diamond Body Prana, Freedom's Cadence, Snake Form and Celestial Tiger Hide, plus the permanent boost of ISoB's control effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T17:03:22-07:00","id":920011,"title":"","content":"Im still not sure if i want to nerf it because it sounds a little awesome. Im going to see how that plays out.<br /> Does anyone have some experience with builds like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T10:04:32-07:00","id":922067,"title":"","content":"Spirit Strengthens the Skinworks for a single attack or for the turn?<br /> Because that can change how good that combo is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T10:41:56-07:00","id":922081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=922067#post922067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit Strengthens the Skinworks for a single attack or for the turn?<br /> Because that can change how good that combo is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an Instant, Reflexive charm, so it only works for a single attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T10:50:18-07:00","id":922089,"title":"","content":"Then its not that OP. It would take a lot of essence to maintain that charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T13:23:33-07:00","id":922188,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sounds like that would be the equivalent of Wonder Woman planting herself and blocking a big attack with her bracers rather than just shrugging off blows throughout a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T14:45:51-07:00","id":922230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=922089#post922089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then its not that OP. It would take a lot of essence to maintain that charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resistance can get costly, though you do get to skip on paying for improving parry/evasion to an extent that a less hardy character couldn't risk. Also, a Resistance-focused character can have Charms such as Essence Gathering Temper, Willpower-Enhancing Spirit, and Front-line Warrior's Stamina that, when well used and with a bit of luck, make that character great at managing their various resources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T07:45:05-07:00","id":922617,"title":"","content":"The only part of that combo that worries me, balance-wise, is Invulnerable Skin of Bronze.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T11:05:55-07:00","id":922734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=922617#post922617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only part of that combo that worries me, balance-wise, is Invulnerable Skin of Bronze.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell <i>is</i> worded in a way that makes this Combo a little suspect, but I think the control effect wouldn't invalidate the whole concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T12:20:22-07:00","id":922776,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that DoOM subtracts 2 successes from Decisive attacks too, not just Withering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T14:43:45-07:00","id":922857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/918274-help-making-a-resistance-focused-solar?p=922776#post922776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind that DoOM subtracts 2 successes from Decisive attacks too, not just Withering.</div> </div> </div> </div>It subtracts two raw damage from the attack, which is importantly distinct from subtracting two successes from the damage roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11517-bozwevial","name":"Bozwevial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}